<section class="faq g-paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="faq-top">
      <div class="faq-aside">
        <div class="eyebrow" data-rv=""><span class="tick">\</span> 06 · Questions</div>
        <h2 data-rv="" style="--d:60ms">What buyers ask us first.</h2>
        <div class="faq-ask" data-rv="" style="--d:180ms">
          <p class="faq-ask-q">Didn’t see yours?</p>
          <a href="/__v9/contact">Ask us anything <span class="ar" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list" data-rv="" style="--d:120ms">
        <details class="faq-item" name="services-faq" open="">
          <summary class="faq-q"
            ><span>Can we combine services?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary
          >
          <div class="faq-a">
            <div>
              <p>
                Most teams use two or three. A stuck role usually goes scorecard, then pipeline review, and only then a
                search. A team scaling in India often goes scorecard library, contract hire, then build, operate,
                transfer. Nothing obliges you to buy the next one.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" name="services-faq">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>How do you price?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
          <div class="faq-a">
            <div>
              <p>
                Recruitment is a percentage of the hire’s annual CTC, due when you hire. Interview as a service is a fee
                per interview, plus a success fee if you hire from it. Advisory and assessment work is a fixed fee,
                agreed in writing before we start. We quote after the first call.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" name="services-faq">
          <summary class="faq-q"
            ><span>Who actually does the work?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary
          >
          <div class="faq-a">
            <div>
              <p>
                Senior experts who have held the job, more than fifty of them across the sectors we cover. Every
                interview, scorecard and assessment is run by one, and you see their name on it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" name="services-faq">
          <summary class="faq-q"
            ><span>What if we’re asking for the wrong thing?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"
            ></span></summary
          >
          <div class="faq-a">
            <div>
              <p>
                We say so on the first call. Sometimes the answer is a two-day scorecard instead of a search. Sometimes
                it’s nothing at all.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" name="services-faq">
          <summary class="faq-q"
            ><span>Do we keep what you make?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary
          >
          <div class="faq-a">
            <div>
              <p>Yes. Scorecards, interview guides and reports are yours, and your team can run them without us.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
